        "question": {
          ":question/id": "d034ca6b-65ae-597f-98ba-e67022eb6282",
          ":question/problem": "Let $b=\\langle 3,-3,-1\\rangle$ and $a=\\langle 3,1,0\\rangle$. Find the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3)(3)+(1)(-3)+(0)(-1)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-3+0}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{19}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
