        "question": {
          ":question/id": "1a4a4177-2e80-5151-9dbd-3bffd258f14b",
          ":question/problem": "Let $b=\\langle -3,0,-4\\rangle$ and $a=\\langle t,0,-2\\rangle$, where $t$ is real. Given that $\\operatorname{comp}_{b}a=\\frac{8}{5}$, find the exact value of $\\operatorname{comp}_{a}b$.\n\n$\\operatorname{comp}_{a}b=$ {{field-1}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Use the known projection to recover the missing component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lVert b\\rVert&=\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}=5,\\\\a\\cdot b&=8-3t,\\\\\\frac{8-3t}{5}&=\\frac{8}{5},\\\\8-3t&=8,\\\\t&=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $a=\\langle 0,0,-2\\rangle$. Reverse the direction of projection, using the magnitude of $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\lVert a\\rVert&=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}=2,\\\\\\operatorname{comp}_{a}b&=\\frac{b\\cdot a}{\\lVert a\\rVert},\\\\&=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4}}=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
